<title>UK: World drug sales up 6 pct in Jan-Aug - IMS survey.</title>
<headline>World drug sales up 6 pct in Jan-Aug - IMS survey.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pharmaceutical sales in ten of the world's leading markets rose six percent year-on-year in local currency terms in January to August, healthcare information specialist IMS International said on Monday.</p>
<p>The figures cover the top seven European markets, plus Japan, the USA and Canada. Separately, IMS for the first time has published a table giving sales in Latin America in the 12 months from July 1995 to June 1996.</p>
<p>IMS detailed retail pharmacy sales as follows, in billions of dollars. Growth rates are in local currency terms.</p>
<p>			  Jan-Aug 96   Jan-Aug 95	Percent growth</p>
<p> U.S.		   37.670	  35.112		  7</p>
<p> Canada		  2.459	   2.324		  5</p>
<p> Germany		11.253	  10.955		  7</p>
<p> France		  9.644	   9.507		  3</p>
